  "description": "TANLEC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H112 Lu4 N12 O16 S6,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Lu1 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu2 (Lu) has 6 O neighbors; Lu3 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu4 (Lu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.487-3.800 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.81-112.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C158H124Lu4N16O16S6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
